.TH TANGSIBLE-HOST 1 "August 2026" "Tangsible" "Tangsible Manual"
.SH NAME
tangsible-host \- everything Tangsible can determine about one host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tangsible host
.I hostname
.RI [ playbook.yml ]
.RI [ "ansible\-playbook args" ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B host
is a standalone, five\-tab view of one inventory host, entirely
separate from the live tree UI \(em there is no run to watch here, just
information gathered up front. If
.I playbook.yml
is omitted, it is resolved the same way
.BR tangsible-run (1)
resolves one (see
.BR tangsible (1)),
though a playbook is only strictly required for the Plays tab; the
others work without one.
.SH TABS
.TP
.B Summary
Live\-gathered facts (FQDN, IP addresses, OS, architecture, RAM,
virtualization, and more), fetched via a throwaway
.B ansible.builtin.setup
task.
.TP
.B Groups
Every inventory group this host belongs to, direct or transitive \(em
a host\-centric view of the group membership an inventory file only
ever expresses the other way around (group \(-> hosts).
.TP
.B Plays
Every play in
.I playbook.yml
that would actually run against this host, narrowed with
.B \-\-limit
.I hostname
.B \-\-list\-tasks \-\-list\-hosts
under the hood. Requires a resolved playbook; reports its own absence
gracefully otherwise.
.TP
.B host_vars
The host's own
.B host_vars
files, if any are found alongside the playbook or inventory.
.TP
.B "Everything known"
The raw
.B ansible\-inventory \-\-host
.I hostname
dump, unfiltered.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Tab / Shift\-Tab
Switch tabs (wraps at both ends).
.TP
.B "Cursor keys / j\-k, Ctrl\-A/E"
Scroll the active tab; Ctrl\-A/E jump to its top/bottom.
.TP
.B /
Search the active tab's text; while a search has at least one match,
.B n / N
jump to the next / previous match.
.TP
.B q / Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.PP
.B Esc
clears an active search if there is one; otherwise it's deliberately
inert, same reasoning as
.BR tangsible-template (1):
only q/Ctrl\-C quit, so idly browsing tabs can never close the program
by reflex.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit, however the view was closed.
.TP
.B 1
A throwaway stub playbook this view depends on internally couldn't be
written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: no
.I hostname
was given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tangsible (1),
.BR tangsible-hosts (1),
.BR tangsible-template (1)
